 "description": "Quick redact list entries and patterns (#1618, round 3 of #1631): the same inputs for the editor's C++ validator (tests/unit/test_text_protocol.cpp) and the MCP server (tests/integration/test_mcp.py). Rules, in order. Terms: a raw line break (\\n, \\r, U+2028, U+2029) is refused; then the value is trimmed of what Qt's QChar::isSpace calls whitespace (U+0085 and U+00A0 included, U+001C not); it must be non-empty, at most 100 code points, and contain a letter or digit. Patterns: a raw line break is refused; then, trimmed the same way, it must be non-empty and at most 500 code points; the raw value must compile and not match empty text. A pattern's shape is not judged: the editor matches in a child process it kills at the deadline, so any pattern PCRE2 compiles is allowed, (* verbs, \\C, lookarounds and back references included. Rules compile and emptyMatch need PCRE2; a checker that has no PCRE2 may leave them to the editor. A compile error is Qt's message with its offset, so its rows give only errorPrefix.",
